---
title: "Helicopter Seeds"
format: html
code-fold: True
---

The seeds from maple, elm and ash trees have curved wings to let them stay in the air longer. The wind will pick up these seeds and carry them to suitable groud. These seeds twirl and spin around. They will then drop and sprount a new tree. Some people call these seeds **helicopter seeds** because they look like and can spin like a propeller.

Here you will learn how to make your own spinner.

1. Fold the middle flap in the opposite direction of the other two flaps. Put the paper clip on the end of the middle flap.

2. Find a maple seed spinner. Drop both spinners from the same height and compare how they spind. Does your spinner work as well as nature's?


